    "note": "Named PMTilesbuilding/templePOI35184810382324 (encoded OSMway438293492) covers the temple main body and eastern appendages near retainedQ4955510 reference74.54887778,26.48732778. Independent named node17599792637901 lies within the main body. Measured long edge gives ENE axis-0.2644885496056613rad; anchor is original reference, heading0/native east-south. The eastern mapped appendages/approach and pictured shrine-behind-open-hall relationship support an approximate east-facing portico. Internal tower/dome/support/door layout, front/back sign and annex allocation remain picture/map estimates, retaining roughly5m/30degree facing uncertainty rather than a surveyed plan. Adjoining wrapping footprint35184809402181 is included as the pictured low pale courtyard gallery after generic multi-storey procedural extrusion obscured the hall during construction inspection. Its temple-complex association, outer room inventory and low roof height are approximate photo/topology allocations; all other buildings stay independent. Retain the standard6m Mapzen DEM/native paths/water and every independent building. Only the named temple shell and its mapped wrapping courtyard gallery are cut with2cm numeric pad minus independent footprints+1mm protection. The occupied temple footprint uses buried contact sides/court cap and a separate raised hall platform, narrow local steps; no whole-precinct slab, flattening or ground/water cutout. Coarse DEM does not resolve courtyard/podium/foundation sections. Levels and entry engineering are explicit visualization fit estimates. Preview uses the host terrain sample at the authored base; ground slope, facade azimuth and final site fit remain review items."
